-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulation 35: DETERMINATION OF EARNINGS FOR BENEFIT PURPOSES.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24, from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt (consolidation current to 2026-09-30). Nothing here is claimed to be verified against
-- the official text.
--
-- HOW IT IS BUILT. Reg 35 answers two questions about one receipt of income: does it count as earnings for a
-- purpose (subsections (2) to (9)), and what is its value (subsections (10) to (16)).
--   * The facts about a receipt are a LIST of the facts that hold (`er3 Fact about the income received`):
--     a fact that is not on the list does not hold. Each limb of the text reads the list for the facts it
--     names, so the limbs can be tested one by one.
--   * "Subject to the other provisions of this section" (35(2)) is encoded as: within (2), and not
--     excluded by (3), (3.1), (4), (5), (6) or (7). The text states no order among the exclusions; none
--     is needed, because every one of them only removes income from the earnings.
--   * "notwithstanding paragraph (7)(b)" (35(2)(d)) is encoded in (7)(b): a payment within (2)(d) is not
--     removed by (7)(b).
-- A judgment the text hands to the Commission (the value in (12), the rental value in (14)) is an input.

§ `The facts about a receipt of income`

-- One constructor per fact a witness could state about the income or about its recipient. They are the
-- facts that limbs (2) to (7) turn on; a limb reads only those it names.
-- src:554 | (2) Subject to the other provisions of this section, the earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of determining whether an interruption of earnings under section 14 has occurred and the amount to be deducted from benefits payable under section 19, subsection 21(3), 22(5), 152.03(3) or 152.04(4) or section 152.18 of the Act, and to be taken into account for the purposes of sections 45 and 46 of the Act, are the entire income of a claimant arising out of any employment, including
