@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(2) to (7) (src:554-584)
DECLARE `er3 Fact about the income received` IS ONE OF
    `er3 income: arising out of any employment`                                                             -- (2) lead-in
    `er3 income: payable in respect of wages, benefits or other remuneration from the proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt employer` -- (2)(a)
    `er3 income: a workers' compensation payment received or to be received`                               -- (2)(b), (4)
    `er3 income: a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments` -- (2)(b), (7)(a)
    `er3 income: a disability pension`                                                                      -- (7)(a)
    `er3 income: a payment under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`                         -- (2)(c)(i), (4), (7)(b)
    `er3 income: that plan is not a group plan under subsection (8)`                                        -- (2)(c)(i), (7)(b)
    `er3 income: a payment under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan`                             -- (2)(c)(ii)
    `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act` -- (2)(c)(iii)
    `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act` -- (2)(c)(iv)
    `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child`            -- (2)(c)(v)
    `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult`            -- (2)(c)(vi)
    `er3 income: a payment from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan provided under a provincial law in respect of the actual or presumed loss of income from employment due to injury` -- (2)(d)
    `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received from that motor vehicle plan` -- (2)(d)
    `er3 income: moneys paid or payable on account of or in lieu of a pension`                              -- (2)(e), (5), (7)(e)
    `er3 income: an indemnity payment under a provincial law because the claimant ceased to work as continuation of work entailed physical dangers` -- (2)(f), (4)
    `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received under that provincial law` -- (2)(f)
    `er3 income: after the week of the injury the claimant accumulated the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act` -- (3)
    `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person who sustained the injury before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act` -- (3.1)
    `er3 income: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`                   -- (6), earnings of 36(9)
    `er3 income: an allowance that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Act` -- (6)
    `er3 income: relief grants in cash or in kind`                                                          -- (7)(c)
    `er3 income: a retroactive increase in wages or salary`                                                 -- (7)(d)
    `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person`                                                    -- (7)(e)(i) and (ii)
    `er3 income: the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act` -- (7)(e)(i)
    `er3 income: the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the benefit period were accumulated after the moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they were received` -- (7)(e)(ii)
    `er3 income: employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act`        -- (7)(f)

-- Whether a fact holds: it is on the list, or it does not hold.
GIVEN fact IS AN `er3 Fact about the income received`
      facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 35 the fact holds of the income` fact facts MEANS elem fact facts

§ `Section 35(1) -- the definitions`

-- src:541 | 35 (1) The definitions in this subsection apply in this section.
-- src:542 | employment means
-- src:543 | (a) any employment, whether insurable, not insurable or excluded employment, under any express or implied contract of service or other contract of employment,
-- src:544 | (i) whether or not services are or will be provided by a claimant to any other person, and
-- src:545 | (ii) whether or not income received by the claimant is from a person other than the person to whom services are or will be provided;
-- src:546 | (b) any self-employment, whether on the claimant's own account or in partnership or co-adventure; and
-- src:547 | (c) the tenure of an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan. (emploi)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(1) "employment" (src:542-547)
GIVEN `any employment, whether insurable, not insurable or excluded, under any express or implied contract of service or other contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any self-employment, whether on the claimant's own account or in partnership or co-adventure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tenure of an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(1) employment` IF
       `any employment, whether insurable, not insurable or excluded, under any express or implied contract of service or other contract of employment`
    OR `any self-employment, whether on the claimant's own account or in partnership or co-adventure`
    OR `the tenure of an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan`

-- "income" has two limbs: what it is (pecuniary or non-pecuniary) and who it comes from.
-- src:548 | income means any pecuniary or non-pecuniary income that is or will be received by a claimant from an employer or any other person, including a trustee in bankruptcy. (revenu)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(1) "income" (src:548)
GIVEN `pecuniary income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `non-pecuniary income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `received or to be received by a claimant from an employer, from a trustee in bankruptcy or from any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(1) income` IF
        (`pecuniary income` OR `non-pecuniary income`)
    AND `received or to be received by a claimant from an employer, from a trustee in bankruptcy or from any other person`

-- src:549 | pension means a retirement pension
-- src:550 | (a) arising out of employment or out of service in any armed forces or in a police force;
-- src:551 | (b) under the Canada Pension Plan; or
-- src:552 | (c) under a provincial pension plan. (pension)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(1) "pension" (src:549-552)
GIVEN `a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arising out of employment or out of service in any armed forces or in a police force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(1) pension` IF
        `a retirement pension`
    AND (   `arising out of employment or out of service in any armed forces or in a police force`
         OR `under the Canada Pension Plan`
         OR `under a provincial pension plan`)

-- "self-employed person has the same meaning as in subsection 30(5)": that definition is reg 30(5)
-- (piece er2); the rules below that need it take it as the fact `the claimant is a self-employed person`.

