    OR `reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` facts
    OR `reg 35(2)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension` facts
    OR `reg 35(2)(f) indemnity payments under a provincial law because continuing to work entailed physical dangers` facts

§ `Sections 35(3) to 35(6) -- payments that are not taken into account`

-- src:570 | (3) Where, subsequent to the week in which an injury referred to in paragraph (2)(d) occurs, a claimant has accumulated the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act, the payments referred to in that paragraph shall not be taken into account as earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(3) (src:570)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(3) a payment in paragraph (2)(d) is not taken into account as earnings after the hours were accumulated` IF
        `reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` facts
    AND `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: after the week of the injury the claimant accumulated the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act` facts

-- src:571 | (3.1) If a self-employed person has sustained an injury referred to in paragraph (2)(d) before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act, the payments referred to in that paragraph shall not be taken into account as earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(3.1) (src:571)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(3.1) a payment in paragraph (2)(d) to a self-employed person injured before the period of section 152.08 is not taken into account as earnings` IF
        `reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` facts
    AND `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person who sustained the injury before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act` facts

-- Subsection (4) is for the purpose of subsection 14(2) only.
-- src:572 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the payments a claimant has received or, on application, is entitled to receive under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan or a workers' compensation plan, or as an indemnity described in paragraph (2)(f), are not earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of subsection 14(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(4) (src:572)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(4) group sickness or disability, workers' compensation and (2)(f) payments are not earnings for the purpose of subsection 14(2)` IF
        purpose EQUALS `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations`
    AND (   (   `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a payment under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan` facts
             AND NOT (`reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: that plan is not a group plan under subsection (8)` facts))
         OR `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a workers' compensation payment received or to be received` facts
         OR `reg 35(2)(f) indemnity payments under a provincial law because continuing to work entailed physical dangers` facts)

-- Subsections (5) and (6) are for the purposes of section 14 (which includes subsection 14(2)).
GIVEN purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35 the purpose is section 14 of the Regulations` IF
        purpose EQUALS `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations`
    OR purpose EQUALS `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under section 14 of the Regulations, other than subsection (2)`

-- src:573 | (5) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the moneys referred to in paragraph (2)(e) are not earnings to be taken into account for the purposes of section 14.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(5) (src:573)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(5) moneys on account of or in lieu of a pension are not earnings for the purposes of section 14` IF
        `reg 35 the purpose is section 14 of the Regulations` purpose
    AND `reg 35(2)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension` facts

-- "the earnings referred to in subsection 36(9)" are earnings paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or
-- separation from an employment (reg 36(9), the same section's next piece of text).
-- src:574 | (6) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the earnings referred to in subsection 36(9) and allowances that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) are not earnings to be taken into account for the purposes of section 14.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(6) (src:574)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(6) lay-off or separation earnings and allowances not deducted under section 16(1) of the Act are not earnings for the purposes of section 14` IF
        `reg 35 the purpose is section 14 of the Regulations` purpose
    AND (   `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment` facts
         OR `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: an allowance that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Act` facts)

§ `Sections 35(7) to 35(9) -- income that is not earnings, and the plan that is not a group plan`

-- (7)(e) The moneys of (2)(e) are not earnings if (i) for a self-employed person they became payable before
-- the beginning of the period of section 152.08 of the Act, or (ii) for any other claimant the hours required by
-- section 7 or 7.1 for the benefit period were accumulated after the moneys became payable and during the period
-- in respect of which they were received.
-- src:580 | (e) the moneys referred to in paragraph (2)(e) if
-- src:581 | (i) in the case of a self-employed person, the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act, and
-- src:582 | (ii) in the case of other claimants, the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the establishment of their benefit period was accumulated after the date on which those moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they received those moneys; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(e) (src:580-582)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension that are not earnings` IF
        `reg 35(2)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension` facts
    AND `reg 35(7)(e)(i) or (ii) the condition for the kind of claimant is met` facts

GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(e)(i) or (ii) the condition for the kind of claimant is met` IS
    IF `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person` facts
    THEN `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act` facts
    ELSE `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the benefit period were accumulated after the moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they were received` facts

-- src:576 | (a) disability pension or a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(a) (src:576)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(a) a disability pension, or a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a workers' compensation claim` IF
       `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a disability pension` facts
    OR `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments` facts

-- (b) is not applied to a payment within (2)(d): that is what "notwithstanding paragraph (7)(b)" in (2)(d) says.
-- src:577 | (b) payments under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan that is not a group plan;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(b) (src:577)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(b) payments under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan that is not a group plan` IF
        `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a payment under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan` facts
    AND `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: that plan is not a group plan under subsection (8)` facts
    AND NOT (`reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` facts)

-- src:578 | (c) relief grants in cash or in kind;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(c) (src:578)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(c) relief grants in cash or in kind` IF
    `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: relief grants in cash or in kind` facts

-- src:579 | (d) retroactive increases in wages or salary;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(d) (src:579)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(d) retroactive increases in wages or salary` IF
    `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: a retroactive increase in wages or salary` facts

-- src:583 | (f) employment income excluded as income pursuant to subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7)(f) (src:583)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7)(f) employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act` IF
    `reg 35 the fact holds of the income` `er3 income: employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act` facts

-- Paragraph (g) of subsection (7) is repealed: reg 35(7)(g) [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 347] (line 584).
-- src:575 | (7) That portion of the income of a claimant that is derived from any of the following sources does not constitute earnings for the purposes referred to in subsection (2):
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(7) (src:575)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(7) the portion of the income derived from an excluded source is not earnings` IF
       `reg 35(7)(a) a disability pension, or a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a workers' compensation claim` facts
    OR `reg 35(7)(b) payments under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan that is not a group plan` facts
    OR `reg 35(7)(c) relief grants in cash or in kind` facts
    OR `reg 35(7)(d) retroactive increases in wages or salary` facts
    OR `reg 35(7)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension that are not earnings` facts
    OR `reg 35(7)(f) employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act` facts

-- (9) "portable": both the benefits and the premium rate stay equivalent on a move to another employer in
-- the same occupation.
-- src:592 | (9) For the purposes of subsection (8), portable, in respect of a plan referred to in that subsection, means that the benefits to which an employee covered by the plan is entitled and the rate of premium that the employee is required to pay while employed by an employer will remain equivalent if the employee becomes employed by any other employer within the same occupation.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(9) (src:592)
GIVEN `the benefits to which an employee covered by the plan is entitled will remain equivalent if the employee becomes employed by any other employer within the same occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate of premium that the employee is required to pay while employed by an employer will remain equivalent if the employee becomes employed by any other employer within the same occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(9) portable` IF
        `the benefits to which an employee covered by the plan is entitled will remain equivalent if the employee becomes employed by any other employer within the same occupation`
    AND `the rate of premium that the employee is required to pay while employed by an employer will remain equivalent if the employee becomes employed by any other employer within the same occupation`

-- (8) The text says a plan "is not a group plan if" it has all six features. It is read as the whole test:
-- a plan with all six is not a group plan and a plan without one of them is a group plan (fork F1).
-- src:585 | (8) For the purposes of paragraphs (2)(c) and (7)(b), a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan if it is a plan that
-- src:586 | (a) is not related to a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer;
-- src:587 | (b) is not financed in whole or in part by an employer;
-- src:588 | (c) is voluntarily purchased by the person participating in the plan;
-- src:589 | (d) is completely portable;
-- src:590 | (e) provides constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources, where applicable; and
-- src:591 | (f) has rates of premium that do not depend on the experience of a group referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(8) (src:585-591)
GIVEN `related to a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `financed in whole or in part by an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `voluntarily purchased by the person participating in the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `completely portable under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provides constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has rates of premium that depend on the experience of a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` IF
        NOT (`related to a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer`)
    AND NOT (`financed in whole or in part by an employer`)
    AND `voluntarily purchased by the person participating in the plan`
    AND `completely portable under subsection (9)`
    AND `provides constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources, where applicable`
    AND NOT (`has rates of premium that depend on the experience of a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer`)

§ `Reg 35 as a whole -- is the income earnings for a purpose?`

-- The question the whole of (2) to (7) answers for one receipt of income: it is within (2) and none of
-- (3), (3.1), (4), (5), (6) or (7) takes it out.
-- src:554 | (2) Subject to the other provisions of this section, the earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of determining whether an interruption of earnings under section 14 has occurred and the amount to be deducted from benefits payable under section 19, subsection 21(3), 22(5), 152.03(3) or 152.04(4) or section 152.18 of the Act, and to be taken into account for the purposes of sections 45 and 46 of the Act, are the entire income of a claimant arising out of any employment, including
-- src:555 | (a) amounts payable to a claimant in respect of wages, benefits or other remuneration from the proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt employer;
-- src:556 | (b) workers' compensation payments received or to be received by a claimant, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments;
-- src:557 | (c) payments a claimant has received or, on application, is entitled to receive under
-- src:558 | (i) a group wage-loss indemnity plan,
-- src:559 | (ii) a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan,
-- src:560 | (iii) a leave plan providing payment in respect of the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act,
-- src:561 | (iv) a leave plan providing payment in respect of the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act,
-- src:562 | (v) a leave plan providing payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child, or
-- src:563 | (vi) a leave plan providing payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult;
-- src:564 | (d) notwithstanding paragraph (7)(b) but subject to subsections (3) and (3.1), the payments a claimant has received or, on application, is entitled to receive from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan provided under a provincial law in respect of the actual or presumed loss of income from employment due to injury, if the benefits paid or payable under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount that the claimant receives or is entitled to receive from the plan;
-- src:565 | (e) the moneys paid or payable to a claimant on a periodic basis or in a lump sum on account of or in lieu of a pension; and
-- src:566 | (f) where the benefits paid or payable under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount that a claimant receives or is entitled to receive pursuant to a provincial law in respect of an actual or presumed loss of income from employment, the indemnity payments the claimant has received or, on application, is entitled to receive pursuant to that provincial law by reason of the fact that the claimant has ceased to work for the reason that continuation of work entailed physical dangers for
-- src:567 | (i) the claimant,
-- src:568 | (ii) the claimant's unborn child, or
-- src:569 | (iii) the child the claimant is breast-feeding.
-- src:570 | (3) Where, subsequent to the week in which an injury referred to in paragraph (2)(d) occurs, a claimant has accumulated the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act, the payments referred to in that paragraph shall not be taken into account as earnings.
-- src:571 | (3.1) If a self-employed person has sustained an injury referred to in paragraph (2)(d) before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act, the payments referred to in that paragraph shall not be taken into account as earnings.
-- src:572 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the payments a claimant has received or, on application, is entitled to receive under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan or a workers' compensation plan, or as an indemnity described in paragraph (2)(f), are not earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of subsection 14(2).
-- src:573 | (5) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the moneys referred to in paragraph (2)(e) are not earnings to be taken into account for the purposes of section 14.
-- src:574 | (6) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the earnings referred to in subsection 36(9) and allowances that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) are not earnings to be taken into account for the purposes of section 14.
-- src:575 | (7) That portion of the income of a claimant that is derived from any of the following sources does not constitute earnings for the purposes referred to in subsection (2):
-- src:576 | (a) disability pension or a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments;
-- src:577 | (b) payments under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan that is not a group plan;
-- src:578 | (c) relief grants in cash or in kind;
-- src:579 | (d) retroactive increases in wages or salary;
-- src:580 | (e) the moneys referred to in paragraph (2)(e) if
-- src:581 | (i) in the case of a self-employed person, the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act, and
-- src:582 | (ii) in the case of other claimants, the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the establishment of their benefit period was accumulated after the date on which those moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they received those moneys; and
-- src:583 | (f) employment income excluded as income pursuant to subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act.
-- src:584 | (g) [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 347]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(2) to (7) (src:554-584)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` IF
        `reg 35(2) the income is within subsection (2), before the exclusions` facts
    AND NOT (`reg 35(3) a payment in paragraph (2)(d) is not taken into account as earnings after the hours were accumulated` facts)
    AND NOT (`reg 35(3.1) a payment in paragraph (2)(d) to a self-employed person injured before the period of section 152.08 is not taken into account as earnings` facts)
    AND NOT (`reg 35(4) group sickness or disability, workers' compensation and (2)(f) payments are not earnings for the purpose of subsection 14(2)` facts purpose)
    AND NOT (`reg 35(5) moneys on account of or in lieu of a pension are not earnings for the purposes of section 14` facts purpose)
    AND NOT (`reg 35(6) lay-off or separation earnings and allowances not deducted under section 16(1) of the Act are not earnings for the purposes of section 14` facts purpose)
    AND NOT (`reg 35(7) the portion of the income derived from an excluded source is not earnings` facts)

§ `Sections 35(10) to 35(16) -- the value of the income`

-- (16) "living quarters means rooms or any other living accommodation".
-- src:605 | (16) For the purposes of this section, living quarters means rooms or any other living accommodation.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(16) (src:605)
GIVEN rooms IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other living accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 35(16) living quarters` IF
    rooms OR `any other living accommodation`

-- (13) The value of living quarters includes the value of any heat, light, telephone or other benefits
-- included with the living quarters.
-- src:602 | (13) The value of living quarters referred to in paragraph (10)(d) includes the value of any heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with the living quarters.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(13) (src:602)
GIVEN `the value of the rooms or other living accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with the living quarters` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(13) the value of living quarters` IS
    `the value of the rooms or other living accommodation` PLUS `the value of any heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with the living quarters`

-- (14) When the Commission determines the value of living quarters, it is the rental value of similar
-- living quarters in the same vicinity or district. That rental value is a fact the Commission finds; it
-- is an input.
-- src:603 | (14) Where the value of living quarters is determined by the Commission, it shall be computed on the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(14) (src:603)
GIVEN `the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(14) the value of living quarters determined by the Commission` IS
    `the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district`

-- (11) and (12). The value of board, living quarters and other benefits is the amount fixed by agreement
-- between the claimant and the employer, if it is reasonable in the circumstances; otherwise it is the
-- value the Commission determines from the monetary value of the benefits. Until the Commission has
-- determined a value, a case that needs it is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:600 | (11) Subject to subsection (12), the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d) shall be the amount fixed by agreement between the claimant and the claimant's employer and shall be an amount that is reasonable in the circumstances.
-- src:601 | (12) Where the claimant and the employer do not agree on the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d), or where the value fixed for those benefits by agreement between the claimant and the claimant's employer is not reasonable in the circumstances, the value shall be determined by the Commission based on the monetary value of the benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(11), (12) (src:600-601)
GIVEN `the claimant and the employer have fixed a value by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value fixed by agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `that value is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value determined by the Commission based on the monetary value of the benefits` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` IS
    IF `the claimant and the employer have fixed a value by agreement` AND `that value is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST `the value fixed by agreement`
    ELSE `the value determined by the Commission based on the monetary value of the benefits`

-- (15) Non-pecuniary remuneration other than living quarters and board furnished by the employer: its
-- value is included in the claimant's income.
-- src:604 | (15) Where the remuneration of a claimant is not pecuniary or is only partly pecuniary and all or part of the non-pecuniary remuneration consists of any consideration other than living quarters and board furnished by the employer, the value of that consideration shall be included in determining the claimant's income.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(15) (src:604)
GIVEN `the remuneration is not pecuniary or is only partly pecuniary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or part of the non-pecuniary remuneration consists of consideration other than living quarters and board furnished by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of that consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(15) the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration to be included in the income` IS
    IF `the remuneration is not pecuniary or is only partly pecuniary` AND `all or part of the non-pecuniary remuneration consists of consideration other than living quarters and board furnished by the employer`
    THEN `the value of that consideration`
    ELSE 0

-- (10)(a) to (c): the income, by the kind of claimant.
-- (a) not self-employed: the income remaining after deducting the expenses incurred for the direct purpose of
--     earning it and the value of any consideration the claimant supplied.
-- (b) self-employed in farming: the gross income, including farming subsidies under a federal or provincial
--     program, remaining after deducting the operating expenses other than capital expenditures. The
--     subsidies are asked apart from the gross income, so that they are counted once.
-- (c) self-employed otherwise: the gross income remaining after deducting the operating expenses other than
--     capital expenditures.
-- src:593 | (10) For the purposes of subsection (2), income includes
-- src:594 | (a) in the case of a claimant who is not self-employed, that amount of the claimant's income remaining after deducting
-- src:595 | (i) expenses incurred by the claimant for the direct purpose of earning that income, and
-- src:596 | (ii) the value of any consideration supplied by the claimant; and
-- src:597 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is self-employed in farming, the gross income from that self-employment, including any farming subsidies the claimant receives under any federal or provincial program, remaining after deducting the operating expenses, other than capital expenditures, incurred in that self-employment;
-- src:598 | (c) in the case of a claimant who is self-employed in employment other than farming, the amount of the gross income from that employment remaining after deducting the operating expenses, other than capital expenditures, incurred therein; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(10)(a) to (c) (src:593-598)
GIVEN kind IS A `er3 Kind of claimant for the value of income`
      `the income received` IS A NUMBER
      `expenses incurred by the claimant for the direct purpose of earning that income` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any consideration supplied by the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the gross income from the self-employment, not counting farming subsidies` IS A NUMBER
      `farming subsidies the claimant receives under any federal or provincial program` IS A NUMBER
      `operating expenses incurred in the self-employment, other than capital expenditures` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(10)(a) to (c) the income from the employment` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `er3 claimant who is not self-employed` THEN
        (`the income received` MINUS `expenses incurred by the claimant for the direct purpose of earning that income`) MINUS `the value of any consideration supplied by the claimant`
    WHEN `er3 claimant who is self-employed in farming` THEN
        (`the gross income from the self-employment, not counting farming subsidies` PLUS `farming subsidies the claimant receives under any federal or provincial program`) MINUS `operating expenses incurred in the self-employment, other than capital expenditures`
    WHEN `er3 claimant who is self-employed in employment other than farming` THEN
        `the gross income from the self-employment, not counting farming subsidies` MINUS `operating expenses incurred in the self-employment, other than capital expenditures`

-- (10)(d) "in the case of any claimant": the value of board, living quarters and other benefits received
-- from the employer is added to whatever (a), (b) or (c) gives. Until that value is known the case is not
-- covered: NOTHING.
-- src:593 | (10) For the purposes of subsection (2), income includes
-- src:599 | (d) in the case of any claimant, the value of board, living quarters and other benefits received by the claimant from or on behalf of the claimant's employer in respect of the claimant's employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 35(10) (src:593) (src:599)
GIVEN `the income from the employment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of board, living quarters and other benefits received from the claimant's employer` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 35(10) the income taken into account, with the value of board, living quarters and other benefits` IS
    CONSIDER `the value of board, living quarters and other benefits received from the claimant's employer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST benefits THEN JUST (`the income from the employment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` PLUS benefits)
